---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: "What does a transparent signature mean?", a: "Only the ink is kept. The paper around it is removed, so the signature can sit on any document without a white box around it." },
  { q: "My signature looks faint or broken after cleaning. What can I do?", a: "Lower the background removal strength, or take a new photo with a darker pen and better light." },
  { q: "Can I use it to sign a PDF?", a: "Yes. Download the PNG and upload it in Sign PDF, or go straight there with the Sign PDF button." },
];
---
<GuideLayout slug="transparent-signature-png" faqs={faqs}>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> sign on white paper with a dark pen, take a photo, and open <a href="/signature-cleaner">Signature Cleaner</a>. The paper is removed automatically. Choose <strong>Transparent PNG</strong> for documents or <strong>White JPG</strong> for forms, and download.</p>

  <h2>Taking a good photo</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use a black or dark blue pen, a little thicker than usual. Gel pens and markers work well.</li>
    <li>Sign on plain white paper with no lines.</li>
    <li>Photograph it in daylight, straight from above, without your phone’s shadow on the page.</li>
    <li>Fill most of the photo with the signature.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step by step</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <a href="/signature-cleaner">pdfsherpa.com/signature-cleaner</a> and select the photo.</li>
    <li>Adjust <strong>Background removal strength</strong> until the paper is gone and the ink stays solid.</li>
    <li>Pick an ink colour: original, black or blue.</li>
    <li>Choose the background: <strong>Transparent PNG</strong> or <strong>White JPG</strong>.</li>
    <li>If a form has a size limit, choose 10KB, 20KB or 50KB.</li>
    <li>Download.</li>
  </ol>

  <AdSlot variant="inline" slot="guide-article" />

  <h2>PNG or JPG?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Transparent PNG:</strong> for placing on PDFs, letters and documents. No white rectangle shows over lines or text.</li>
    <li><strong>White JPG:</strong> for job and exam portals that ask for a signature image in JPG with a size limit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where to use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sign PDFs with <a href="/sign-pdf">Sign PDF</a> using the Upload option.</li>
    <li>Add it to a document with <a href="/edit-pdf">Edit PDF</a> as an image.</li>
    <li>Resize to exact pixels for a form with <a href="/resize-image">Resize Image</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keep your signature safe</h2>
  <p>
    A clean signature image can be misused if it falls into the wrong hands. PDFSherpa processes it in your browser and never uploads it.
    Don’t post it publicly, and only send it to people and portals you trust.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
